<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andragoras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 238 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andragoras was the Seleucid governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> who declared himself independent around 245 BCE and issued his own coins. Around 238 BCE he was overthrown and killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsaces-i">Arsaces I</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parni">Parni</a>, whose seizure of Parthia began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsacid-dynasty">Arsacid dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a>.</p></div>
